<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO cuts Van Ommeren to Hold.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO cuts Van Ommeren to Hold.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of March 26 research.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>    Van Ommeren     Transport     80.80   ABN AMRO Hoare Govett</p>
<p>COMMENT: Hold (from Buy). 1998 estimates reduced as little sign of upturn in petrochemical storage and risk of slowdown in chemical storage. 1998 net profit estimate downgraded by 6 pct and EPS estimate by 9 pct. Downturn in chemicals market in 1998 likely to be offset by new capacity, acquisitions and likely disposal of non-core assets. However, positive view on company's strategic development remains. Expect share to trade in 75-85 guilders range over next six months.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS     P/E    P/CF   Dividend yield</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)     6.06    14.8   6.5    3.1</p>
<p>    1997		  6.77    11.9   6.0    3.3</p>
<p>    1998		  7.25    11.1   5.8    3.6</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
